.worktrees/
.claude/worktrees/

# Annunaki rotation backups — created by /annunaki-attack Step 1 before clearing
# errors.jsonl. Historical-only; safe to age out locally, not for tracking.
.claude/annunaki/errors.jsonl.bak.*

# Annunaki benign-trace stream (#625) — high-churn, machine-generated forensic
# dispatch/diagnostic traces split out of errors.jsonl so /annunaki stops
# over-counting them as errors. Local diagnostic aid only; never committed.
.claude/annunaki/traces.jsonl
.claude/annunaki/traces.jsonl.bak.*

# Annunaki error stream (#948) — same machine-local, hook-appended, high-churn
# property as traces.jsonl above and session_handoff.md below; it was the odd
# one out. The PostToolUse monitor appends on EVERY Bash call, so a `git push`
# dirties the tree of the very push it is observing, and the pre-push hooks
# reject it with "files were modified by this hook" on a fully GREEN suite.
# With concurrent agents it is strictly unwinnable: their Bash calls append
# continuously, so the parent repo can never present a clean tree while any
# agent is running. A gate that cries wolf on a green suite trains the reflex
# to reach for --no-verify — the exact habit the no-force rule (#684) exists to
# suppress. /annunaki and /annunaki-attack read the log from disk, so both keep
# working; cross-clone history is the deliberate trade (the W23 retro already
# proposed pruning this log at wrapup, so its full history is not load-bearing).
.claude/annunaki/errors.jsonl

# In-repo project memory (#732). The CURATED corpus (MEMORY.md + topic files) IS
# version-controlled and loaded via the `@.claude/memory/MEMORY.md` import in
# CLAUDE.md. Only the per-session, machine-local Stop-hook handoff is excluded —
# it churns every ~5min and is session/machine-specific, not shared knowledge.
.claude/memory/session_handoff.md

# Obsidian editor workspace state (local, not shared)
ontology/.obsidian/
